          <li>Swami Muktibodhananda, <i>Swara Yoga: The Tantric Science of Brain Breathing</i>. Munger: Bihar School of Yoga, 1984. Includes the text and a translation of the Shiva Swarodaya.</li>
          <li>A. L. Pendolino et al., “The nasal cycle: a comprehensive review”, <i>Rhinology Online</i> 1 (2018). <a href="https://www.rhinologyonline.org/Rhinology_online_issues/2018/18021_Pendolino.pdf">rhinologyonline.org</a>.</li>
          <li>D. A. Werntz, R. G. Bickford, F. E. Bloom, D. S. Shannahoff-Khalsa, “Alternating cerebral hemispheric activity and the lateralization of autonomic nervous function”, <i>Human Neurobiology</i> 2 (1983).</li>
          <li>A. Price and R. Eccles, “Nasal airflow and brain activity: is there a link?”, <i>The Journal of Laryngology &amp; Otology</i> 130 (2016): 794–799.</li>
          <li>Profile of Ma Shakti Devpriya, The Shakti Multiversity: <a href="https://www.shaktimultiversity.com/master-detail/ma-shakti-devpriya">shaktimultiversity.com</a>.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
